{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqiu0hk3hxq","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Abstain-by-default exists to avoid the 'over-deliberation tax' measured in bench/report-v2..v7","summary":"The gates default to abstain because the benchmark found that on self-solvable tasks every orchestrator-ON arm did MORE work than OFF — injecting context the model didn't need is not free: it pays consult-overhead C (cache cost to hold the graph) AND nudges the model into extra deliberation. The whole point of the context-need gate is to suppress that tax by injecting only on a confident empirical match. This is why 'predict by default / inject only when confident' is a hard project stance, not mere caution.","created_by":null,"valid_from":"2026-06-18T01:39:13.251Z","vec":[-0.07528380304574966,-0.026755448430776596,-0.03538551181554794,0.07049810141324997,0.027935614809393883,-0.028044315055012703,0.05458693206310272,0.014794827438890934,0.014539207331836224,0.068269744515419,-0.0012608334654942155,-0.038876503705978394,0.0013868877431377769,0.007745354901999235,0.04168472811579704,0.025907566770911217,0.14609868824481964,-0.10059851408004761,0.0192209891974926,-0.04263238608837128,0.062120117247104645,-0.015785207971930504,0.0109501788392663,-0.0007041206699796021,0.05111072584986687,-0.07796645909547806,-0.11206085979938507,0.027222713455557823,0.09611859172582626,-0.017186585813760757,-0.02449260652065277,0.09143278002738953,-0.0077613345347344875,-0.024087538942694664,-0.0709100216627121,0.010698141530156136,0.011019834317266941,0.002848610980436206,0.027588002383708954,0.016929389908909798,0.025707440450787544,-0.0018394093494862318,-0.03918665647506714,0.015497824177145958,0.014405712485313416,-0.007989669218659401,0.007113763131201267,-0.1315189152956009,-0.031239405274391174,0.0059972116723656654,-0.08243512362241745,0.009602767415344715,0.06336063146591187,-0.0549054890871048,-0.03581571951508522,0.015992024913430214,-0.03437578305602074,-0.004558742046356201,-0.01184707414